lib/WWW/Zitadel/Error.pm defines 4 packages (Error, Error::Validation, Error::Network, Error::API). Only the first has our $VERSION; the three sub-classes are versionless in code. dzil build/test warns: "3 provide map entries did not map to .pm files". Per getty-perl-release-author-getty, one package per file: BumpVersionAfterRelease rewrites only the first $VERSION, so a manual per-package $VERSION would freeze while META bumps -> silent code/META disagreement. Correct fix = split into Error/Validation.pm, Error/Network.pm, Error/API.pm and update t/00-load.t. Pre-existing since 0.001 (not a 0.002 regression), non-blocking. NOTE: mirror the split in async twin p5-net-async-zitadel.

